      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, Benoît. I agree that we should cover both architectures in this change. The revised patch uses a dedicated post-doorbell flush, with `sfence` on x86-64 and `dsb st` on Arm64, following rdma-core.\n\nOn ConnectX-5 Ex, the x86-64 UET SEND completion p50 went from 357 µs to 66 µs with one SEND outstanding per PDC. On BlueField-3, both versions completed 3,600 tagged UET ping-pong exchanges over the physical mlx5 port, with a TAP behind VPP. Median RTT was 235 µs before and 240 µs after the change, and the p99 varied across runs. The BF3 result gives us functional validation on Arm64.",
